          "text": "The pattern indexes as a **primitive tetragonal** cell with \\(a \\approx 6.5635\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 9.0628\\) \u00c5. The strongest diagnostic reflections are:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 9.75\u00b0 | 001 |\n| 13.49\u00b0 | 100 |\n| 16.67\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 19.11\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 19.58\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 23.84\u00b0 | 102 |\n| 27.15\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 27.49\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 32.02\u00b0 | 211 |\n| 32.60\u00b0 | 103 |\n| 33.69\u00b0 | 202 |\n| 38.78\u00b0 | 220 |\n| 39.75\u00b0 | 004 |\n\nThe 001 and 100 superstructure reflections rule out the cubic \\(Fm\\bar 3m\\) K\u2082PtCl\u2086 parent. The best average model is **\\(P4/mmm\\), Z = 2**, with complementary axial F/Cl ordering and 25:75 equatorial Cl/F disorder. The split equatorial coordinates below enforce chemically reasonable Sn\u2013F and Sn\u2013Cl distances of approximately 1.95 and 2.42 \u00c5.\n\n```cif\ndata_K2SnCl3F3_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Indexed and chemically constrained from Cu Kalpha1 powder diffraction'\n_chemical_name_common                 'dipotassium tin chloride fluoride'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'K2SnCl3F3'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Cl3 F3 K2 Sn'\n_chemical_formula_weight              360.25\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 2\n\n_cell_length_a                        6.5635\n_cell_length_b                        6.5635\n_cell_length_c                        9.0628\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          390.4\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P 4/m m m'\n_space_group_IT_number                123\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         3.065\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nK   1\nSn  4\nCl -1\nF  -1\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nSn1       Sn  1a  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000  1.00  0.50\nSn2       Sn  1d  0.50000  0.50000  0.50000  1.00  0.50\nK1        K   4i  0.00000  0.50000  0.25000  1.00  1.20\n\nF_ax1     F   2g  0.00000  0.00000  0.21516  1.00  1.10\n\nCl_eq1    Cl  4j  0.26070  0.26070  0.00000  0.75  1.00\nF_eq1     F   4j  0.21008  0.21008  0.00000  0.25  1.20\n\nCl_ax2    Cl  2h  0.50000  0.50000  0.76703  1.00  0.90\n\nF_eq2     F   4k  0.71008  0.71008  0.50000  0.75  1.20\nCl_eq2    Cl  4k  0.76070  0.76070  0.50000  0.25  1.00\n```\n\nThis CIF is the **diffraction-average structure**. A locally fully ordered mer-\\([\\mathrm{SnCl_3F_3}]^{2-}\\) arrangement, distributed among rotational domains, is effectively homometric with this 25:75 occupational model in the present powder data. The exact split-site coordinates and local Cl/F correlations would require neutron diffraction, total scattering, or single-crystal data; the cell, tetragonal metric, and axial ordering are substantially better determined.",
